their foreign workers.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Rodrigo Duterte ruled fit to stand trial by ICC judges</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df554c6296edd2eec13035085cb35d542e87e3a4cf0e9724f51e4cca17240cd4</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/rodrigo-duterte-ruled-fit-to-stand-trial-by-icc-judges/a-79599372--793387d40a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/rodrigo-duterte-ruled-fit-to-stand-trial-by-icc-judges/a-79599372?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Judges at the International Criminal Court said Rodrigo Duterte was fit to understand the charges at his trial, which is set to begin in November. His legal team argued that he suffers from cognitive deficiencies.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU envoy in Beijing for talks to calm trade tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e1e84d4710a63832ee12dbdba3280b525efb252b7783d87ce481301cded1230</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-envoy-in-beijing-for-talks-to-calm-trade-tensions/a-79598713--6570dc66b587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-envoy-in-beijing-for-talks-to-calm-trade-tensions/a-79598713?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU trade envoy said he hoped to make progress in tackling the bloc's "unsustainable" trade imbalance with China. Beijing called for trade disputes to be resolved through equal dialogue.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India faces water and power shortages after weak monsoon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f547f8791b1d1018463d56a90efd9b4239bf38826a14bbfb242f057f211f28dc</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T14:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540--3ab74afcb33c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-faces-water-and-power-shortages-after-weak-monsoon/a-79599540?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A weak monsoon in India is hitting farmers, water supplies and the power system, while raising wider questions about increasingly erratic rainfall and the economic costs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea warns of AI-aided hacking after bank data breaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec0425816692f33c7a0a7519e05a1b190bae9f131963cc8a7093a63f608bc804</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922--3290ee11faa1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-warns-of-ai-aided-hacking-after-bank-data-breaches/a-79592922?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Seoul is alarmed after a recent breach of South Korean banks' cyber defenses that reportedly involved AI-assisted hacking. Officials warn such methods could be used to also target other sectors and government agencies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Opposition doubles down against poll chief after detentions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:68fe098aaca1cbad8d368173187f57f5c2bb9339cf558a766a60dc2d3e4234dc</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T12:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-doubles-down-against-poll-chief-after-detentions/live-79587554--49a24ea9d897.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-opposition-doubles-down-against-poll-chief-after-detentions/live-79587554?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's opposition alliance is gearing up for another day of protests after demonstrating lawmakers were detained for the second time. Meanwhile, India is seeking to repatriate its nationals working in Russian military.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea recalls Ukraine ambassador amid POW dispute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e23d6ba6bb7f624cbf3af19c0793a503bcbf995b9aafcc99dc84cba55f70175</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511--9732a38bcd21.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-recalls-ukraine-ambassador-amid-pow-dispute/a-79590511?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Korea has said it will recall its ambassador to Ukraine. Seoul is upset about a transfer of North Korean prisoners of war being made public knowledge at the UN and had demanded — but not received — an apology.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China's Golden Week reveals cautious consumer spending despite travel surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f14a69adc1fdc63e9788d94225ebc6f2c7b9ec66a9d512c6a7195d85beb0b823</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254--362469c231fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chinese visitors are returning from trips after the 13-day Golden Week holiday. Their subdued spending has raised fresh questions about domestic demand in the world's second-largest economy.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Southeast Asia's haze crisis: Have lessons been learned?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7bb3b1a7678acbcfe50f0456b63ef1420a2d33cf0628910de12e4d5852cb5b7c</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992--f0834d091bdd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/southeast-asia-s-haze-crisis-have-lessons-been-learned/a-79564992?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven years after catastrophic fires prompted promises of tougher action, Southeast Asia is again choking on transboundary haze, raising questions about whether the region has learned the lessons of 2015.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>What China's new military foothold in Laos means for Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1cb420b3c2b3da2be2ab69ded183a38073e829a7f78ee02c036f77ee40623b05</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259--642cd34d5dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says its new Laos facility will train pilots. Analysts see a broader signal: China's growing military presence in mainland Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A brutal assault reignites fears over women's safety in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe7f6cb5bce7aa02fc3277cd12dcece65f8de19777b343b0a9a88a31a7bc8a45</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471--bceecddefb45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-brutal-assault-reignites-fears-over-women-s-safety-in-india/a-79501471?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A string of sexual violence cases has revived questions about women's safety in India, fueling fear, protests and demands for action.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Lawyer of Junaid Hafeez, a Pakistai scholar imprisoned for 13 years, is hopeful for his release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec738f833b1fd8d2a5c5a937420b44296756c09e9a3650d95343aee5a0bdb032</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T13:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207--6c93b577eab6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/lawyer-of-junaid-hafeez-a-pakistai-scholar-imprisoned-for-13-years-is-hopeful-for-his-release/a-79490207?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A former Fulbright scholar, Junaid Hafeez was sentenced to death under Pakistan's controversial blasphemy laws. His family and lawyer told DW there is now hope a court will overturn the conviction.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea has recently completed two road bridges easing transport to strategic allies Russia and China</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:32b6364eb60b241f4a1c766784daed2445f33576d15b276e8ac8ec1b69d3ac36</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-/a-79473981--09998bc65869.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-has-recently-completed-two-road-bridges-easing-transport-to-strategic-allies-russia-and-china/a-79473981?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two recently opened bridges are expected to ease trade and transport between North Korea and its powerful neighbors. The new connections come as Pyongyang builds strategic ties with China and Russia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Women and children displaced by Nepal's floods say safe housing, privacy and stability remain out of reach</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae3f0b02e37b702af046f0b2b434d0214372570718592d22912b045d54c91255</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-/a-79474014--5ad51afec87b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-and-children-displaced-by-nepal-s-floods-say-safe-housing-privacy-and-stability-remain-out-of-reach/a-79474014?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Families living in temporary shelters in northern Nepal say safety and privacy remain out of reach as concerns about trafficking and abuse mount.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Global trade weathers Iran, Ukraine and Trump's tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd13b8a07c7a543d98dd011a38adddf7879bfd2855a29fe75b1317bfab279448</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643--538fe77d9a72.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/global-trade-weathers-iran-ukraine-and-trump-s-tariffs/a-79352643?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past six years, COVID, two wars and Donald Trump's tariffs have shaken world trade. With globalization already stalling, is this a temporary shock or the start of a great reversal?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Three-way battle for power in world chess: Who will be elected FIDE president in Samarkand?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48601a0841cb6a0ed9185cbeccf6bcf0351c2e8e14ea6f0e8014f4319fa9e430</id><updated>2026-10-09T06:22:11Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T18:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301--bc60333e85fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/three-way-battle-for-power-in-world-chess-who-will-be-elected-fide-president-in-samarkand/a-79413301?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The era of Russian presidents is coming to an end at the World Chess Federation (FIDE). Two Germans and one Kazakh are up for election. Among the issues at play are money, Kremlin influence, and unanswered questions.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
